    "created_at": "2016-08-25T15:09:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-25T15:09:20Z",
    "body": "General comment: I always felt this API was a bit clumsy. I kind of wish we used a dictionary. \"ImageEncodeOptions\" or something like that.  I understand we can't break away from quality for backwards compatibility reasons, but would it be reasonable to introduce an overload that takes a dictionary? and maybe someday we'll be able to deprecate \"quality\".  The reason I ask is that we will most likely want to add more options in the near future to control color space, and bit depth.  Eventually maybe more options, like image orientation, and whether or not to encode the alpha channel.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "reactions": {
