    "created_at": "2016-08-25T15:17:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-25T15:17:26Z",
    "body": ">  I understand we can't break away from quality for backwards compatibility reasons, but would it be reasonable to introduce an overload that takes a dictionary?\n\nIMO yes, although it would be a slight breaking change. We'd want to move from any + type testing to double (or unrestricted double?) in order to make it possible to introduce an overload. Probably nobody is relying on `\"0.9\"` being ignored instead of being converted to a quality indicator, so it's probably fine.\n\nAlternately we could continue down the custom bindings route to maintain more strict backward compat.\n\nThere's also #379 in the related area.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
